The samples were three synthetic polyisoprene elastomers reticulated with dicumyl peroxide at 443 K, made into 2.8 mm thick plates, with Tg adjusted using liquid paraffin or resin. The slider roughness was 1.3 µm rms, the abrasive grain size was nominally 23 µm, and the glass track was used to minimize interdiffusion-related changes in shear strength with contact age. Dynamic mechanical measurements spanned 0.1-750 Hz, which overlaps the proposed 550 Hz sampling rate but is not stated to be a friction trace sampling rate.
